# x-host-browser-page: desktop wiring (the lead applies it). No HOST_METHOD row is needed:
# the method name is HOST_BROWSER_PAGE, exported by host/browser-page-report.ts (as HOST_STATE_SET is by browser-tabs.ts).

[browser/host-presentation.ts] (the function that returns createBrowserRemoteControl({...}))
  Add a second argument to that call:
    createBrowserRemoteControl({ ...existing host object... }, { onStreamedPageChanged: options.onStreamedPageChanged })
  and add to that function's options type:
    onStreamedPageChanged?: (sessionId: string) => void;
  browser/host.ts forwards its own `onStreamedPageChanged` option into it.

[host/index.ts] (createDesktopHost, beside createBrowserTabsReporter)
  import { createBrowserPageReporter } from './browser-page-report';
  const pageReport = createBrowserPageReporter(connection, (sessionId) => options.browser().view.streamedPage(sessionId));
  The browser host is constructed with: onStreamedPageChanged: (sessionId) => pageReport.changed(sessionId)
  (streamedPage is the member createBrowserRemoteControl already returns; the `view` the host options carry must expose it.)
  On connection close / host role release: pageReport.stop().
